// Reactivity S5 (hardening) — an `effect` has no readable value: it is a side-effecting subscription,
// not a cell or a derivation. Calling `.get()` on one is rejected with the same "no method" error any
// built-in gives for a method it lacks (`.dispose()` is the only method an `Effect` handle carries).
// The kind-guarded dispatch means the `(Effect, "get")` pair never reaches the read path — it falls
// through to E0005, identically on both backends.
// expect: error E0005 at 11:1
// expect: exit 1
use std.reactive.{signal, effect}
sig = signal(0)
e = effect(fn() { sig.get() })
e.get()
